# Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds, bridge (figure 108.3)
# The top row is the tune: a repeated D over the chords (a ninth chord on C, a thirteenth on F),
# sliding down to B-flat ("B-f|lat" typed across the bar line, so held into bar 8). The bridge
# pivots from B-flat to G (C is V-of-V in B-flat and IV in G).
# The last bar is the switch to 4/4, counted "D 2 3 4" in the typed chart. Pollack says the 3/4
# quarter equals the new eighth, so that bar is written 8 of the old beats long, each count 2 beats.
#? Check that the 4/4 bar really lasts 8 of the bridge's 3/4 beats when played (tempo change).
meter 3/4
key Bb

system
voice "Melody"   | D5 | - | - | - | - | - | - Bb4 | - |
chords           | B-flat{I} | - | C{V-of-V} | - | F{V} | - | B-flat{I} | - |

system
voice "Melody"   | D5 | - | - | - C5 B4 | <8> A4*2 -*2 -*2 -*2 |
chords           | C{V-of-V = G: IV} | - | G{G: I} | - | <8> D{G: V}*8 |
words            | r | r | r | r | <8> 1*2 2*2 3*2 4*2 |
